            <p class={`text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed [overflow-wrap:anywhere] ${CODE}`} set:html={inlineCodeHtml(e.corps)} />
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
              <strong>What it changed.</strong> <span class={CODE} set:html={inlineCodeHtml(e.change)} />
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </CaseStudySection>

    <CaseStudySection eyebrow="The problem with V1" id="le-probleme-de-la-v1">
      <h3 data-intertitre class={H3}>A lost trial, on November 7</h3>
      <p>
        V1 delivered reviewed, tested and shipped lots, but at a price its
        own surveys showed. On November 7, 2026, 1.62, the last release
        of V1, redid 8 real requests already delivered, against Claude Code alone,
        from the same commit. It lost on time and on tokens; what the blind
        judge and the hidden tests said about it is on the page
        <a href="/case-studies/pourquoi-cadence/" hreflang="fr">Pourquoi cadence</a> <span class="whitespace-nowrap text-ink-muted">(in French)</span>.
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {v1Mesures.map((m) => (
          <div data-v1-chiffre={m.id} data-source={m.source} class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-paper-elevated p-borne-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-lg text-claude">{insecable(m.valeur)}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">{insecable(m.quand)}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{insecable(m.legende)}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-ink-muted [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
              Source: <a href={doc(m.source)} target="_blank" rel="noopener">↗ {m.source}</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h3 data-intertitre class={H3}>Five causes, four measured</h3>
      <p>
        The design document of cadence 2 (<a href={doc(DESIGN)} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="[overflow-wrap:anywhere]">↗ {DESIGN}</a>,
        November 7, 2026) puts the defeat down to five causes. It measures four of them; the second,
        C2, is only described there, with no figure:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3 list-none">
        {v1Causes.map((c) => (
          <li data-v1-cause={c.id} data-source={DESIGN} class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-paper-elevated p-borne-5">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-claude mb-2">{c.id}</p>
            <h4 class="text-base font-medium text-ink mb-1.5">{c.titre}</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">{insecable(c.corps)}</p>
            {!c.mesuree && <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-muted"><strong>Described, not measured.</strong></p>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <Callout titre="What V1 leaves behind">
        <p>
          Cadence 2 keeps what V1 really brought: the plan tied to the
          commits, the test gate, verified delivery, the short review of the
          diff, the screenshot review of screens and the in-browser check
          after delivery.
        </p>
      </Callout>

      <h3 data-intertitre class={H3}>The decisions of cadence 2</h3>
      <p>
        Each decision says which cause it answers. When its effect is measured,
        the measurement is given; when it is not yet, that is said too.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-4 list-none">
        {v2Decisions.map((d) => (
          <li data-v2-decision={d.id} data-causes={d.causes.join(" ")} class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-paper-elevated p-borne-5">
            <h4 class="text-base font-medium text-ink mb-1">{d.titre}</h4>
            <p data-repond class="font-mono text-xs text-claude mb-2">
              {d.causes.length ? `Answers ${d.causes.join(", ")}` : "Answers none of the five causes"}
            </p>
            <p class={`text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed [overflow-wrap:anywhere] ${CODE}`} set:html={inlineCodeHtml(insecable(d.corps))} />
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink leading-relaxed">
              <strong>{d.mesure ? "Measured effect." : "Not measured yet."}</strong>{" "}
              {insecable(d.effet)}
              {d.id === "run" && <> <a href="/case-studies/pourquoi-cadence/" hreflang="fr">Read the bench evidence</a> <span class="whitespace-nowrap text-ink-muted">(in French)</span>.</>}
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 list-none">
              {d.preuves.map((pr) => (
                <li data-source={pr.fichier} class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-ink-muted [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
                  Source: <a href={doc(pr.fichier)} target="_blank" rel="noopener">↗ {pr.fichier}</a> ({insecable(pr.quand)})
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-paper-elevated p-borne-5">
        What is still missing: the survey of a lot's time (25 min and 266 k tokens
        in V1) has not been redone for <code>cadence run</code>. The comparison of
        V1 and cadence 2 on real work remains to be done; the evidence that
        exists comes from the bench, on a few requests.
      </p>
    </CaseStudySection>

